  "preamble": "Palatalization and affrication of [t] to the alveolo-palatal affricate [tɕ] before the high front vowel /i/ or another front vowel. Old Japanese ti became [tɕi], Proto-Slavic *t before front vowels developed into Polish ć [tɕ], and Middle Korean ti became modern ci [tɕi] in the 17th–18th-century Korean palatalization.",
